in\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciated nonetheless! I'm often surprised when people haven't heard of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T22:44:37-08:00","id":1032491,"title":"","content":"Looks cool, thanks for sharing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T22:27:18-08:00","id":1036444,"title":"","content":"Well, this certainly saves me work. Thanks a bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:32:46-08:00","id":1036844,"title":"","content":"The problem I see with Vicissitude is that it feels like it should be Vigor/Protean based but I'm sure we've had at least 2 Gangrel with Vigor bloodlines so I don't want to add another. Nos or Daeva could both make good parent clans (body horror or obsessive artists) but everyone wants to tie them to Ventrue because of their WoD lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:37:47-08:00","id":1036870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1030292-bloodline-fiendish-forms-tzimisce?p=1036844#post1036844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I see with Vicissitude is that it feels like it should be Vigor/Protean based but I'm sure we've had at least 2 Gangrel with Vigor bloodlines so I don't want to add another. Nos or Daeva could both make good parent clans (body horror or obsessive artists) but everyone wants to tie them to Ventrue because of their WoD lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for more Gangrel bloodlines; they actually have the fewest, if I recall.<br /> <br /> This is ultimately more of an attempt to port in the CWoD Tzimisce minus the metaplot/Masquerade setting details (as suits the purposes of my AP, really). If there were to be something official, I'd actually like to see something more like the Khaibit, where it takes inspiration from the old clan, but it does its own thing. You could have a really interesting bloodline of spies, which is a niche the Tzimisce oddly never really seemed to hit upon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:31:08-08:00","id":1036902,"title":"","content":"If you haven't read it, Paul O'Conner's Strigoi is actually an incredibly good requiem revision of the Tzimisce - and comes in two distinct bloodlines for both Ventrue and Nosferatu. I, personally, remade this for my own use at one point (not the story - the mechanics) to be compatible for 2e. Like you, I gave them protean - the Nos and the Ventrue - and had devotions that felt more in line with one of their types use disciplines one side would have - but the devotions were available to both sides, just more common in one than the other due to it being more in path. I believe this is the original - not sure if you can use it, but I've always loved it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.scribd.com/document/39443247/Vampire-The-Requiem-Bloodline-The-Strigoi-by-Paul-O-Connell\" target=\"_blank\">The Strigoi</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:39:15-08:00","id":1036905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1030292-bloodline-fiendish-forms-tzimisce?p=1036902#post1036902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't read it, Paul O'Conner's Strigoi is actually an incredibly good requiem revision of the Tzimisce - and comes in two distinct bloodlines for both Ventrue and Nosferatu. I, personally, remade this for my own use at one point (not the story - the mechanics) to be compatible for 2e. Like you, I gave them protean - the Nos and the Ventrue - and had devotions that felt more in line with one of their types use disciplines one side would have - but the devotions were available to both sides, just more common in one than the other due to it being more in path. I believe this is the original - not sure if you can use it, but I've always loved it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.scribd.com/document/39443247/Vampire-The-Requiem-Bloodline-The-Strigoi-by-Paul-O-Connell\" target=\"_blank\">The Strigoi</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Strigoi quite a bit. It's a neat take on the two sides of the clan. I don't think I've ever used their mechanics, but I have this feeling I name-dropped them in a chronicle at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T02:28:56-08:00","id":1037097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1030292-bloodline-fiendish-forms-tzimisce?p=1036902#post1036902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you haven't read it, Paul O'Conner's Strigoi is actually an incredibly good requiem revision of the Tzimisce - and comes in two distinct bloodlines for both Ventrue and Nosferatu. I, personally, remade this for my own use at one point (not the story - the mechanics) to be compatible for 2e. Like you, I gave them protean - the Nos and the Ventrue - and had devotions that felt more in line with one of their types use disciplines one side would have - but the devotions were available to both sides, just more common in one than the other due to it being more in path. I believe this is the original - not sure if you can use it, but I've always loved it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.scribd.com/document/39443247/Vampire-The-Requiem-Bloodline-The-Strigoi-by-Paul-O-Connell\" target=\"_blank\">The Strigoi</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, was this written before the Strix were a thing? I assumed so because I couldn't find the word Strix there.<br /> <br /> In that case, let's see... We have a bloodline with the same namesake as the infamous Owls. Now, let's look back in some of the more disliked bits of VtM lore, where Vicissitude is a manifestation of alien parasites, called Souleaters. Aliens in WoD are generally assumed to be something similar in nature to Umbrood, aka spirits. Now let's remember that the Strix are also something similar to spirits, but different. They have Breath-Eating abilities, and in older myths the words &quot;soul&quot;, &quot;life&quot; and &quot;breath&quot; are often used interchangeably.<br /> <br /> This all fits perfectly together. The Strigoi must be a bloodline of vampires infected by the smoke-and-blood pseudomatter of the Dark Places that the Strix are spawned from!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:58:16-08:00","id":1038716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1030292-bloodline-fiendish-forms-tzimisce?p=1037097#post1037097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, was this written before the Strix were a thing? I assumed so because I couldn't find the word Strix there.<br /> <br /> In that case, let's see... We have a bloodline with the same namesake as the infamous Owls. Now, let's look back in some of the more disliked bits of VtM lore, where Vicissitude is a manifestation of alien parasites, called Souleaters. Aliens in WoD are generally assumed to be something similar in nature to Umbrood, aka spirits. Now let's remember that the Strix are also something similar to spirits, but different. They have Breath-Eating abilities, and in older myths the words &quot;soul&quot;, &quot;life&quot; and &quot;breath&quot; are often used interchangeably.<br /> <br /> This all fits perfectly together. The Strigoi must be a bloodline of vampires infected by the smoke-and-blood pseudomatter of the Dark Places that the Strix are spawned from!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that would be because the Strix are, in fact, not Strigoi :-p Strigoi are the romanian word for vampires. Strix, or Striges, are a roman phenomena regarding owls of ill omen - while they use the same etymology enough to be referenced together in wiki pages, they are actually two separate things as far as I can tell. I'd be more concerned about the name &quot;Strigoi VII&quot; and it's ties with VII than with Strix :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T00:03:51-08:00","id":1038786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1030292-bloodline-fiendish-forms-tzimisce?p=1038716#post1038716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, that would be because the Strix are, in fact, not Strigoi :-p Strigoi are the romanian word for vampires. Strix, or Striges, are a roman phenomena regarding owls of ill omen - while they use the same etymology enough to be referenced together in wiki pages, they are actually two separate things as far as I can tell. I'd be more concerned about the name &amp;quot;Strigoi VII&amp;quot; and it's ties with VII than with Strix :-p</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Guess I learn something new every day. Still, it's still fun to think they are related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}